**Uniform Asymptotic Expansions for Large Orders**

When \(n\) is large and positive

**9.10.37**

\[\begin{array}{l}{\rm ber},(\nu z)+i\ {\rm bei},(\nu z)\sim\\ \frac{e^{\Phi}}{\sqrt{2\pi\nu z}}\left(\frac{xe^{\Phi zt/t}}{1+\xi}\right)^{ \ast}\left\{1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{u_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\right\} \end{array}\]

**9.10.38**

\[\begin{array}{l}{\rm ker},(\nu z)+i\ {\rm kei},(\nu z)\\ \sim\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{2\nu\xi}}\ e^{-\Phi t}\left(\frac{xe^{\Phi zt/t}}{1+\xi} \right)^{-\nu}\left\{1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(-\right)^{k}\frac{u_{k} (\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\right\}\end{array}\]

**9.10.39**

\[\begin{array}{l}{\rm ber}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu z)+i\ {\rm bei}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu z)\\ \sim\sqrt{\frac{\xi}{2\pi\nu}}\ \frac{e^{\Phi t}}{x}\left(\frac{ze^{\Phi zt/t}}{1+\xi}\right)^{-\nu}\left\{1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{u_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\right\} \end{array}\]

**9.10.40**

\[\begin{array}{l}{\rm ker}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu z)+i\ {\rm kei}^{\prime}_{\prime}(\nu z)\\ \sim\!-\sqrt{\frac{\pi\xi}{2\nu}}\ \frac{e^{-\Phi t}}{x}\left(\frac{ze^{\Phi zt/t}}{1+\xi}\right)^{-\nu}\left\{1+\sum\limits_{k=1}^{\infty}\left(-\right)^{k}\frac{u_{k}(\xi^{-1})}{\nu^{k}}\right\} \end{array}\]

where

**9.10.41**

\[\begin{array}{l}\xi=\sqrt{1+ix^{3}}\end{array}\]

and \(u_{k}(t),t_{k}(t)\) are given by **9.3.9** and **9.3.13.** All fractional powers take their principal values.

